WEBVTT

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:36.200
Thanks for having me.

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:38.590
It was our pleasure.

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:42.590
So you're leaving us tomorrow?

00:01:42.670 --> 00:01:46.150
Why don't you stay
a while longer?

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:49.530
I'd love to, but I have
to prepare for Bon Festival.

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:52.780
Grandpa comes back once a year,

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:57.000
and he'd be lonely if
I weren't there for him.

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:01.970
You're right.

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:07.740
Besides, now I understand
this one's situation.

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:09.080
What do you mean?

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:13.240
He obviously needs to mature,
but please look after him.

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:14.110
Grandma!

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.520
I'd really appreciate it.

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:17.360
Oh, please...

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:19.580
You! Show some respect.

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:20.850
Thank you.

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:40.300
I'm leaving.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.910
- Oh Yusaku!
- Huh?

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:45.410
Please buy me
a ticket for the bullet train

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:47.200
and a gift for the family.

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:48.450
Sure.

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:54.680
Don't lose this.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.080
What would be a good gift?

00:02:57.230 --> 00:02:59.700
As long as it's from Tokyo,
it doesn't matter.

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:01.300
Good morning.

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:02.950
'Morning.

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:04.170
'Morning.

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:06.100
You're going home
to the country?

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:07.570
Yes. Tomorrow.

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:12.380
You're leaving? I thought
you wanted to be buried here?

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:16.510
Don't even think about
pocketing the change!

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:20.740
Thank you all for having me.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:22.550
We're going to miss you.

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:25.710
We must send you off
properly with a party.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:28.390
For me? Thank you.

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:31.160
Geez.

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:34.570
Godai?

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:35.460
Yes?

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:39.040
Are you job-hunting
all day again?

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:41.430
No. I only have
one appointment today.

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:45.600
Great. Would you go
shopping with me after that?

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:48.080
R-Really?

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:52.820
I want to give Grandma
a gift for being so nice.

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:54.580
You don't need to do that.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:56.480
I'd like to.

00:03:56.570 --> 00:04:01.490
Okay. I should be done by
noon, so I'll call you then.

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:02.360
Bye!

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:04.920
Good luck.

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:20.100
Godai? What do you think
of this for Grandma?

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:24.800
I think it's nice
but rather pricey...

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:27.440
I'm sorry it's taking a while
for me to find something.

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:29.020
It's okay with me.

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:31.920
If you don't mind,
I better look some more.

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:33.650
Take your time.

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:52.470
The least expensive ones
are 300 000 yen.

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:55.690
Looking for
an engagement ring?

00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:57.820
W-Well-

00:05:57.980 --> 00:06:00.880
Three months' salary
is generally considered

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.220
a good guideline to spend
on an engagement ring.

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:05.480
May I suggest
one of these, perhaps?

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:07.130
No, I...

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:08.610
Thanks for waiting.

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:10.590
L-Let's go.

00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:11.960
Godai?

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:12.790
Hurry!

00:06:13.130 --> 00:06:14.060
Sir?!

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:16.940
Is something wrong?

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:18.230
N-No.

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:36.440
Three months' salary
is generally considered

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:38.860
a good guideline to spend
on an engagement ring.

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:43.240
Are you okay?

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:45.190
Y-Yes.

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:48.270
- Manager.
- Yes?

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:52.180
I'm going
to find a good job.

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:53.190
Huh?

00:06:55.170 --> 00:06:55.730
Yes.

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:24.900
You want some plum wine, too?

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:33.120
Good?

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:51.920
For being the manager's dog,
you're a greedy one.

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:55.860
I put my heart and soul
into this plum wine.

00:07:56.060 --> 00:07:57.680
I hope you appreciate it.

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:13.770
You're quite a lush,
aren't you?!

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:27.880
Thank you for
carrying everything.

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:28.990
Sure.

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:31.820
Manager?

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:32.710
Yes.

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:36.800
I had a great time today.

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:39.400
It was nice to go
shopping, just you and I.

00:08:40.810 --> 00:08:42.540
I guess we'd never
done this before.

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:49.470
Looks like rain.
Let's hurry.

00:09:02.460 --> 00:09:03.820
Welcome back!

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:05.500
Welcome!

00:09:10.670 --> 00:09:12.570
Soichiro! Down!

00:09:13.810 --> 00:09:15.100
Hm? You smell like alcohol.

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:16.000
Alcohol?

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:19.870
How could you, Grandma?!

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:23.550
Stop it! Down!

00:09:23.630 --> 00:09:26.550
Stupid dog! Down! Stop that!

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:28.120
Don't do that!

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:30.300
Bad dog!

00:09:30.820 --> 00:09:32.760
Are you okay, Manager?

00:09:55.550 --> 00:10:00.450
Let us begin our
Farewell-to-Grandma party.

00:10:00.690 --> 00:10:04.450
How nice of you to have
a farewell party for me.

00:10:04.630 --> 00:10:07.290
C'mon, Yusaku. Wipe that
frown off your face.

00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:08.420
What frown?

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:10.960
Forget it.

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:13.000
He's always like that.

00:10:14.070 --> 00:10:16.410
Um, about what
happened earlier...

00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:19.770
I didn't do it on purpose.

00:10:20.020 --> 00:10:21.670
I know. I'm sorry.

00:10:22.650 --> 00:10:23.470
Godai?

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:30.910
Manager?

00:10:33.030 --> 00:10:33.920
Why doesn't each of us say

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:35.820
a few parting words
to the grandmother?

00:10:36.090 --> 00:10:37.390
Y-Yes.

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:40.680
Let's see.

00:10:41.430 --> 00:10:45.030
My grandparents passed away
when I was a little girl,

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:46.130
so being with you,

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:48.060
I imagine what my own
grandmother may have been like.

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:50.000
She's so serious.

00:10:50.070 --> 00:10:53.170
You didn't expect a joke
out of her, did you?

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:58.640
Grandma, this is a gift for you.
I hope you can use it.

00:10:58.710 --> 00:11:00.330
May I open it?

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:01.010
Sure.

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:06.120
Nice!

00:11:06.290 --> 00:11:07.170
Tasteful!

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:11.490
I hope you like it.

00:11:13.170 --> 00:11:15.090
Manager, you're a good person.

00:11:16.140 --> 00:11:16.820
Thank you.

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:19.350
Akemi, a few words, please.

00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:22.690
Uh... Please come back again soon.

00:11:23.170 --> 00:11:26.600
Women are perennials!
May you blossom again!

00:11:27.550 --> 00:11:28.910
My turn, then.

00:11:30.940 --> 00:11:35.340
Stewed hijiki, potato
nikkorogashi, kinpira burdock,

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:37.880
eggplant shigiyaki,
mixed sushi.

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:38.840
What the heck?

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:41.520
He invited himself over
for dinner all the time.

00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:43.450
Everything was delicious.

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:46.210
I look forward to your
homemade dishes next time.

00:11:48.670 --> 00:11:50.900
Thank you, everyone.
Thank you.

00:12:00.340 --> 00:12:03.140
I feel tipsy.
I think I drank too much.

00:12:04.210 --> 00:12:05.300
Aw...

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:12.100
Blackout!

00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:13.520
Who's got candles?

00:12:13.590 --> 00:12:16.000
I think the
lightning hit close by.

00:12:16.050 --> 00:12:18.670
M-Manager, don't be scared.

00:12:19.270 --> 00:12:20.290
I'm right here.

00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:27.290
When did he get here?

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:30.430
Hey, stop that!

00:12:30.780 --> 00:12:31.600
Soichiro!

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:36.510
Get down, Soichiro.

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:38.540
You're still drunk
aren't you?

00:12:39.420 --> 00:12:41.040
Let go of her!

00:12:42.710 --> 00:12:44.700
Come here, Soichiro.

00:12:45.390 --> 00:12:48.810
Good boy. Have some more.

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:51.890
Hey! Don't give him anymore!

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:55.220
A dog can feel lonely, too.
I know.

00:12:55.740 --> 00:12:58.350
Let's drink together
until the rain stops, huh?

00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:29.770
What'll I do with you, Soichiro?

00:13:34.050 --> 00:13:36.040
He sure loves you.

00:13:36.130 --> 00:13:38.310
It's more than that.

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:42.260
He must be madly in
love with the manager.

00:13:42.600 --> 00:13:44.450
Something bothering you?

00:13:44.560 --> 00:13:45.730
Not really.

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:48.320
Dogs are just like people.

00:13:48.570 --> 00:13:50.930
He wants the attention
of the one he loves.

00:13:51.800 --> 00:13:54.290
Don't be shy to
seek the same.

00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:55.770
Leave me alone!

00:13:55.850 --> 00:13:57.750
Come on, young man.

00:13:57.880 --> 00:14:00.500
How about a drink to
chase away your crankiness?

00:14:02.050 --> 00:14:03.950
Another drink, Soichiro?

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:06.770
Grandma, I think
he's had enough.

00:14:08.230 --> 00:14:10.390
They say dogs become
just like their owners,

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:12.860
but you're nothing like her.

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:17.280
Was your husband a bad drunk?

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:17.790
Huh?

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:21.890
Oh, yeah. Soichiro was
actually your husband's dog.

00:14:22.300 --> 00:14:25.320
Please! My husband
never drank.

00:14:25.900 --> 00:14:27.870
He was a cool
and collected man.

00:14:28.670 --> 00:14:30.510
He was never this annoying!

00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:38.900
He must have been
a good husband.

00:14:39.320 --> 00:14:39.880
Yes.

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:44.990
With his head on
your lap like that,

00:14:45.060 --> 00:14:46.650
you're like a married couple!

00:14:47.630 --> 00:14:50.550
Soichiro, let's go downstairs.

00:14:54.800 --> 00:14:56.290
Come on, Honey.

00:14:56.380 --> 00:15:00.200
No! I don't want
you two alone!

00:15:02.150 --> 00:15:03.270
Get away from her!

00:15:03.850 --> 00:15:05.010
Godai?

00:15:08.490 --> 00:15:11.440
Is he like that
every time he's drunk?

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:13.440
Yeah. Pretty much.

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:29.230
Go! Go at it! Go!

00:15:46.780 --> 00:15:48.040
Let's see...

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:57.810
Let's go, Yusaku.
It's almost one.

00:15:58.100 --> 00:15:59.310
I got a hangover.

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:02.760
So what?  Since you're
not job-hunting today,

00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:05.820
you can carry my
stuff to the station.

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:09.010
If I were well enough
to carry your luggage,

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:10.770
I'd be out job-hunting!

00:16:18.590 --> 00:16:21.650
You're so pathetic!

00:16:24.760 --> 00:16:26.180
Take care of yourself.

00:16:26.270 --> 00:16:27.950
I'll come back
to see you again.

00:16:29.100 --> 00:16:32.000
Yusaku? What're you doing?
Hurry up!

00:16:35.060 --> 00:16:37.650
It's not like you had
that much to drink.

00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:40.870
Look at Soichiro. He's fine.

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:43.510
- Grandma?
- Huh?

00:16:44.570 --> 00:16:46.840
Let me walk you
to the station, too.

00:16:46.990 --> 00:16:49.170
You will? Thank you.

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:52.470
Are you all right?

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:55.270
I can carry her things.

00:16:55.760 --> 00:16:57.120
I'm all right.

00:16:57.190 --> 00:16:57.890
But...

00:16:58.100 --> 00:16:59.050
Really.

00:16:59.290 --> 00:17:00.890
You're two years apart.

00:17:07.230 --> 00:17:08.660
Hey!

00:17:08.930 --> 00:17:13.300
Grandma! Wait!
We're all coming!

00:17:13.440 --> 00:17:14.440
CLOCK HILL STATION
Yay!

00:17:14.440 --> 00:17:18.660
CLOCK HILL STATION

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:23.230
Take care, Grandma.

00:17:23.510 --> 00:17:25.200
Come back with more plum wine.

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:29.080
Grandma, please come
and visit us again.

00:17:29.250 --> 00:17:30.780
Yes. Thank you.

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:34.710
Thanks so much for coming
all the way here.

00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:36.450
Godai?

00:17:41.930 --> 00:17:44.760
Thanks for coming with me.

00:17:44.880 --> 00:17:46.640
Well, with Godai like that...

00:17:46.700 --> 00:17:48.610
He's so pathetic.

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:50.220
Let's pretend
we don't know him.

00:17:56.790 --> 00:17:58.620
Are you okay, Godai?

00:17:58.950 --> 00:18:00.440
T-Thanks for asking.

00:18:21.170 --> 00:18:23.730
Thank you for looking
after my grandson.

00:18:23.820 --> 00:18:25.310
We're used to him.

00:18:25.940 --> 00:18:27.490
- Yusaku?
- Huh?

00:18:29.360 --> 00:18:31.080
Don't forget to eat right.

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:33.970
And call as soon
as you find a job.

00:18:34.060 --> 00:18:34.580
All right?

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:37.290
Take care, Grandma.

00:18:55.710 --> 00:18:59.230
Niigata-bound Toki will be
departing from platform 19.

00:18:59.550 --> 00:19:02.140
Please stand behind
the white line.

00:19:13.660 --> 00:19:15.990
There has been an accident
involving the overhead line

00:19:16.070 --> 00:19:17.030
in the Takasaki vicinity.

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:21.420
This train will be delayed.
Thank you for your patience.

00:19:30.740 --> 00:19:33.340
Thanks for waiting with me.

00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:35.340
We have nothing
else to do anyway.

00:19:36.210 --> 00:19:38.440
They said they can't estimate
how long it'll be.

00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:42.380
I just wanna go home
and sleep.

00:19:43.420 --> 00:19:47.380
Hey! I bought us some beer!

00:19:48.070 --> 00:19:50.720
No sense just waiting
with nothing to do.

00:19:50.800 --> 00:19:51.950
You're right!

00:19:53.260 --> 00:19:55.160
Cheers!

00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:57.600
Let's party!

00:19:59.440 --> 00:20:03.310
It's not often you get
a hangover this bad.

00:20:03.740 --> 00:20:07.340
Godai, drink with us.

00:20:07.980 --> 00:20:08.780
No thanks.

00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:13.090
Please! You're
disturbing the others!

00:20:13.180 --> 00:20:15.410
So what? We're bored.

00:20:15.590 --> 00:20:17.480
Wanna join us?

00:20:18.990 --> 00:20:20.950
I don't know them.
I don't know them.

00:20:23.600 --> 00:20:25.360
Godai, where are you going?

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:28.150
The smell of beer's
making me sick.

00:20:30.670 --> 00:20:32.760
Shall we move far away?

00:20:36.970 --> 00:20:39.030
Where are you going, Manager?

00:20:40.120 --> 00:20:43.730
Look, Grandma.
That's Godai's trick.

00:20:43.820 --> 00:20:46.240
He pretends to be sick so he
can wrap himself around women.

00:20:46.330 --> 00:20:47.380
So sneaky!

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:49.350
How dare he!

00:20:57.800 --> 00:20:58.650
Got 'im!

00:21:07.150 --> 00:21:08.840
Thank you for your patience.

00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:13.080
Niigata-bound Toki is
now departing From platform 19.

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:17.310
Manager, why don't you leave
him alone and drink with us?

00:21:17.410 --> 00:21:19.880
Don't even talk about drinking.

00:21:19.980 --> 00:21:23.470
I didn't know Godai was
such a lightweight.

00:21:23.560 --> 00:21:26.510
You can get rid of a hangover
by drinking some more.

00:21:26.760 --> 00:21:29.560
Grow some balls, will you?

00:21:31.990 --> 00:21:32.620
Huh?

00:21:34.960 --> 00:21:37.010
I'm sorry you had
to see me like this.

00:21:37.110 --> 00:21:39.630
Don't be sorry.
Besides, if those people-

00:21:41.080 --> 00:21:42.000
Godai?!

00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:46.870
Her luggage and gifts!

00:21:49.590 --> 00:21:53.010
Let's party on until
the next Bullet Train!

00:21:53.090 --> 00:21:54.110
Yeah!

00:22:03.190 --> 00:22:05.360
How did you let this happen?

00:22:06.070 --> 00:22:06.920
When we went to pick her up,

00:22:07.000 --> 00:22:08.760
we found her luggage
and gifts but no Grandma.

00:22:08.840 --> 00:22:10.060
We were worried sick.

00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:12.180
So Grandma got there okay?

00:22:12.280 --> 00:22:13.610
I'll put her on.

00:22:13.970 --> 00:22:15.070
Yusaku?

00:22:15.150 --> 00:22:16.190
I forgot to tell you,

00:22:16.280 --> 00:22:18.570
but the manager's
too good for you!

00:22:18.650 --> 00:22:19.300
Huh?

00:22:19.390 --> 00:22:22.880
But don't you give up on her.

00:22:23.010 --> 00:22:25.440
Grandpa had to try
very hard to get me.

00:22:25.710 --> 00:22:27.970
Sometimes, persistence is key.

00:22:28.290 --> 00:22:29.150
Grandma...

00:22:29.220 --> 00:22:33.450
I asked your neighbors
to look after you

00:22:33.530 --> 00:22:34.790
and gave them
some money for booze.

00:22:34.870 --> 00:22:35.250
Huh?

00:22:36.100 --> 00:22:38.490
Yusaku? Are you listening?

00:22:39.460 --> 00:22:41.370
I get it. I get it now.

00:22:42.200 --> 00:22:43.830
Let's party!

00:22:43.970 --> 00:22:46.760
Where's Godai?

00:22:46.850 --> 00:22:49.170
It's just not
as fun without him.

00:22:49.780 --> 00:22:52.260
But we can't stop now.

00:22:52.350 --> 00:22:53.810
She gave us money
to drink, after all.

00:22:58.750 --> 00:23:00.180
How are you feeling?

00:23:02.490 --> 00:23:04.400
They're unstoppable.

00:23:04.650 --> 00:23:07.170
If you like, please feel free
to rest In my apartment.

00:23:13.730 --> 00:23:15.100
Do you mean that?

00:23:15.230 --> 00:23:17.530
Sure. You have more job
interviews tomorrow, don't you?

00:23:17.840 --> 00:23:19.420
You need to go to bed early.

00:23:19.610 --> 00:23:20.830
Bed?

00:23:21.170 --> 00:23:24.260
I-I thought maybe
you'd like some tea.

00:23:24.350 --> 00:23:27.170
Manager, I-

00:23:27.390 --> 00:23:28.400
I...

00:23:29.120 --> 00:23:30.050
Godai?

00:23:45.920 --> 00:23:48.000
What? Yagami's father?

00:23:48.080 --> 00:23:49.920
He's the Director of Recruiting.

00:23:49.990 --> 00:23:51.650
What a golden opportunity!

00:23:51.730 --> 00:23:53.250
It's an elite firm, isn't it?

00:23:53.320 --> 00:23:55.490
A connection is what
really matters!

00:23:55.560 --> 00:23:59.470
Next time:
"A Midsummer Night's Dream!
Godai Finds a Job!"

00:23:59.530 --> 00:24:02.320
Looks like you've
found that connection!
